REMOTE SERVER

Purpose:  create authorized_keys, set ACLs, and (optionally) restart SSH service.
ALL COMMNANDS RUN ON POWERSHELL

START--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# create ~/.ssh
$ssh = "$env:USERPROFILE\.ssh"
$auth = Join-Path $ssh 'authorized_keys'
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ssh | Out-Null

# paste your PUBLIC key (single line from remote_backup.pub on your PC)
Write-Host "Paste your PUBLIC KEY (single line) and press Enter:"
$pub = Read-Host
Set-Content -Path $auth -Value $pub -NoNewline -Encoding ascii

# secure ACLs so OpenSSH accepts them
icacls $ssh /inheritance:d | Out-Null
icacls $ssh /grant "$env:USERNAME:(F)" /t | Out-Null
icacls $ssh /remove "Authenticated Users" "BUILTIN\Users" "Everyone" /t | Out-Null
icacls $auth /inheritance:d | Out-Null
icacls $auth /grant "$env:USERNAME:(R)" | Out-Null

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------NEXT STEP

Restart the SSH service (Admin PowerShell on TALLYSERVER):

net stop sshd
net start sshd

